.TH "ofti" "1" "2026\-07\-29" "OFTI" "User Commands"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
ofti \- scriptable OpenFOAM case utilities and terminal interface
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBofti\fR [\fB\-h\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-plain\fR] [\fB\-V\fR] [\fICASE\fR]
.PP
\fBofti knife\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti run\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti watch\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti plot\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti bundle case\fR \fICASE\fR \fB\-\-output\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti bundle set\fR \fICASE\fR.\&.\&.\& \fB\-\-output\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti bundle extract\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR \fB\-\-to\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti result\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [options]
.PP
\fBofti plugins\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [options]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
OFTI is a CLI\-first convenience layer over foamlib and native OpenFOAM tools.\&
Without a non\-interactive command it opens the curses interface for \fICASE\fR, or
the current directory.\& The CLI and TUI call the same services.\&
.PP
Commands do not silently overwrite case data.\& Mutating operations expose an
explicit apply, output, snapshot, or destination option.\& Machine consumers
should request \fB\-\-json\fR and check both the process exit status and the returned
\fBschema_version\fR.\&
.PP
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Show command help.\& Every command and subcommand provides its own help.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-debug\fR
.RS 4
Enable debug logging and verbose error reports.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-plain\fR, \fB\-\-no\-tty\fR
.RS 4
Never enter curses.\& An explicit non\-interactive command is required.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print the OFTI version.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
\fBknife\fR
.RS 4
Inspect, validate, compare, edit, adopt, stop, and report on cases.\& Important
subcommands include \fBdoctor\fR, \fBpreflight\fR, \fBcheckpoint\fR, \fBphysical\fR,
\fBcompare\-fields\fR, \fBmetric\fR, \fBmanifest\fR, \fBregistry\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBcurrent\fR, \fBadopt\fR,
\fBset\fR, \fBcriteria\fR, \fBeta\fR, \fBreport\fR, and \fBcampaign\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBrun\fR
.RS 4
Run solvers and tools, smoke\-test portable case copies, resize parallel runs,
generate parameter matrices, and execute queues.\& Subcommands are \fBtool\fR,
\fBsolver\fR, \fBsmoke\fR, \fBrestart\-plan\fR, \fBresize\-parallel\fR, \fBmatrix\fR,
\fBparametric\fR, \fBqueue\fR, \fBqueue\-summary\fR, and \fBstatus\fR.\&
\fBrun smoke \-\-iterations N\fR disables adaptive stepping in the smoke copy and
requires exactly N logged steps, a clean solver exit, a nonzero final
checkpoint, and readable output.\& Parallel smoke requires a common checkpoint
across every requested processor; \fB\-\-reconstruct\fR additionally proves
reconstruction.\& \fBrestart\-plan\fR is read\-only and reports common/partial times,
MPI\-size consistency, and the ordered mutation plan.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwatch\fR
.RS 4
Inspect logs and control tracked jobs.\& Subcommands are \fBjobs\fR, \fBstatus\fR,
\fBlog\fR, \fBattach\fR, \fBstart\fR, \fBpause\fR, \fBresume\fR, \fBinterval\fR, \fBoutput\fR, \fBrun\fR,
\fBstop\fR, and \fBexternal\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBplot\fR
.RS 4
Render terminal plots from solver logs and criteria data.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBbundle case\fR, \fBbundle set\fR, \fBbundle extract\fR
.RS 4
Create portable minimal case or campaign archives.\& \fBbundle extract\fR detects
the embedded manifest, verifies all hashes, and restores either archive kind.\&
Case bundles retain native OpenFOAM layout and can optionally start the
restored case.\& A case\-local run manifest and its build digest are embedded
when available.\& Set extraction is staged before restored cases are published.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBresult\fR
.RS 4
Pack and unpack result or restart state.\& Processor state is included only
when the selected time is complete across every processor directory.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBplugins\fR
.RS 4
List installed plugin entry points or diagnose load and registration
failures.\& Reports source, distribution/version, and registered knife, run,
watch, result, progress, preset/profile, and bundle\-hint surfaces.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH OUTPUT AND EXIT STATUS
.PP
Human\-readable output is concise.\& \fB\-\-table\fR selects stable tabular output where
supported.\& \fB\-\-json\fR emits a machine envelope with \fBschema_version\fR, \fBcommand\fR,
\fBok\fR, warnings, errors, and command data.\& Diagnostics go to standard error.\&
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Success, or a report\-only diagnostic completed.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
Operational failure, failed check when requested, or solver failure.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB2\fR
.RS 4
Invalid arguments, unknown preset/profile, or usage validation failure.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBOFTI_CONFIG\fR
.RS 4
Path to the user TOML configuration.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBOFTI_JSON_VERSION\fR
.RS 4
Default JSON envelope version.\& Version 1 remains the compatibility default.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBOFTI_WATCH_STALE_AFTER_SECONDS\fR
.RS 4
Age threshold for STALE_LOG and NO_PROGRESS evidence.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBOFTI_ENABLE_REAL_CASE_TESTS\fR
.RS 4
Enable opt\-in tests that launch real OpenFOAM commands.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBWM_PROJECT_DIR\fR, \fBWM_PROJECT_VERSION\fR, \fBFOAM_RUN\fR
.RS 4
OpenFOAM environment hints used for tool and tutorial discovery.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH FILES
.PP
\fBCASE/ofti.\&toml\fR
.RS 4
Case\-local configuration.\& CLI flags and environment variables take priority.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\(ti/.\&config/ofti/config.\&toml\fR
.RS 4
Default user configuration when \fBOFTI_CONFIG\fR is unset.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBCASE/.\&ofti/jobs.\&json\fR
.RS 4
Atomic tracked\-job registry.\& Repair it from durable run identities with
\fBofti knife registry repair CASE\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBCASE/.\&ofti/runs/*.\&json\fR
.RS 4
Durable run identity records used for process ownership recovery.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBCASE/runs/*\fR
.RS 4
Case\-local immutable run manifests and optional input snapshots.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBCASE/.\&ofti/queues/*\fR
.RS 4
Queue summaries and append\-only event journals.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBCASE/.\&ofti/transactions/*\fR
.RS 4
Snapshots, full diffs, before/after hashes, and rollback evidence for atomic
multi\-dictionary edits.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Inspect a case without starting the TUI:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti \-\-plain knife preflight CASE \-\-json
ofti knife status CASE \-\-table
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reduce a field or extract stationarity from sampled output:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti knife metric CASE \-\-field p \-\-time latest \-\-reduction mean \-\-json
ofti knife metric CASE \-\-field wallHeatFlux \-\-patch wall \-\-reduction max \-\-json
ofti knife metric CASE postProcessing/probes/0/p \-\-value\-column 1 \-\-json
ofti knife metric CASE \&'postProcessing/sets/*/line_p\&.xy\&'
  \-\-threshold 0\&.3 \-\-value\-column 1 \-\-window 20 \-\-max\-span 1e\-4 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start, inspect, and safely stop a solver:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti watch start CASE \-\-background
ofti watch jobs CASE \-\-table
ofti watch stop CASE \-\-signal TERM
.fi
.RE
.PP
Resize a stopped decomposed run after validating its checkpoint:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti knife checkpoint CASE \-\-common \-\-np auto \-\-json
ofti run restart\-plan CASE \-\-to 8 \-\-json
ofti run resize\-parallel CASE \-\-to 8 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Inspect plugin discovery:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti plugins list \-\-json
ofti plugins doctor \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Move a minimal case to another host:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti bundle case CASE \-\-output case\&.ofti\&.tar\&.gz \-\-smoke \-\-json
ofti bundle case CASE \-\-output case\&.ofti\&.tar\&.gz
  \-\-run\-manifest RUN/manifest\&.json \-\-json
ofti bundle extract case\&.ofti\&.tar\&.gz \-\-to CASE_COPY \-\-run \-\-background \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Move a case campaign and run it through the normal queue:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti bundle set \-\-cases\-file cases\&.txt \-\-cases\-root \&.
  \-\-output study\&.ofti\-set\&.tar\&.gz \-\-json
ofti bundle extract study\&.ofti\-set\&.tar\&.gz \-\-to STUDY \-\-json
ofti run queue STUDY/CASE_A STUDY/CASE_B \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate a dictionary\-aware sweep and package it for an HPC handoff:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti run parametric CASE \-\-grid\-axis \&'application=simpleFoam,pisoFoam\&'
  \-\-output\-root runs \-\-bundle\-set study\&.ofti\-set\&.tar\&.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a sequential queue that continues after a failed case:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
ofti run queue CASE_A CASE_B \-\-max\-parallel 1 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.PP
Use \fBofti knife doctor CASE\fR for case\-structure diagnostics and \fBofti knife
preflight CASE\fR for launch prerequisites.\& \fBofti watch status CASE\fR reports
stable reason codes plus STARTING, SOLVING, WRITING, STALLED_LOG,
PARTIAL_CHECKPOINT, MPI_FAILED, and FINISHED run states.\& Destructive recovery
is never inferred: restart planning is read\-only and checkpoint quarantine
previews by default and requires \fB\-\-apply\fR.\&
.PP
.SH LIMITATIONS
.PP
OpenFOAM directives and code streams that foamlib cannot evaluate remain
best\-effort.\& Real MPI lifecycle validation depends on a host that permits MPI
launcher sockets.\& Scheduler integration is not a supported generic interface.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
